 ## Overview
-Coherent Multiresolution Isosurface Ray Tracing optimizes interactive isosurface extraction from large volumetric datasets stored in octrees [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of low spatial coherence in large volumes by grouping neighboring rays into 2x2 packets and adapting coherent traversal algorithms to hierarchical grid structures [S1, unofficial]. Unlike single-ray tracers or coherent kd-tree tracers for meshes, this method leverages the inherent multiresolution level-of-detail (LOD) of the octree to maintain coherence on complex data, allowing interactive performance on commodity CPUs [S1, unofficial].
+Coherent Multiresolution Isosurface Ray Tracing optimizes interactive isosurface extraction from large volumetric datasets stored in octrees [S1, unofficial]. It solves the problem of low spatial coherence in large volumes by grouping neighboring rays into 2x2 packets and adapting coherent traversal algorithms to hierarchical grid structures [S1, unofficial]. Unlike single-ray tracers or coherent kd-tree tracers for meshes, this method leverages the inherent multiresolution level-of-detail (LOD) of the octree to maintain coherence on complex data, allowing interactive performance on commodity CPUs [S1, unofficial]. Smoothing of isosurfaces between resolutions is acceptable and can be desirable in visualization [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the coherent kd-tree isosurface ray tracer of Wald et al. and extends it to octree volumes, differing from siblings like [Cell-Based First-Hit Ray Casting](1039-cell-based-first-hit-ray-casting.md), [Hybrid Strategy for Interactive High Resolution Isosurface Ray Tracing](3697-hybrid-strategy-for-interactive-high-resolution-isosurface-r.md), and [Interactive High Resolution Isosurface Ray Tracing](4093-interactive-high-resolution-isosurface-ray-tracing.md) by explicitly combining packet-based coherence with octree LOD traversal [S1, unofficial].
 
